From 38677ae2788888d0ad0deaf8710eae4afb838a7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:07:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_complete: refuse a ship review verdict
 recorded outside the card's dispatched worker run

Defect agent-9eea612942 (recurrence agent-8a7de4b89f). Supervisor chat 20261111_090650_1247e7 completed ship
review card t_01a1cce808ae7ea0 (PR #1133 @9b3f5ad0) itself with a subagent's verdict: run 29959 started and
ended in the same second, no worker spawn, no reviewer session. `hermes-core-wt ship --review-task` refused it
hours later ("its latest run did not complete; no completed review record"), and a fresh worker review had to be
filed. The review-contract gate checked only the metadata shape, never who was completing.

kanban_review_contract.independence_refusal: on a card whose body names a core-fork pull (states_contract
implies it), a review result carrying a verdict key, completed by a caller with no dispatched worker run for the
card (`_worker_run_id(tid)` is None), is refused with the new rejection class `review_independence`. Nothing
changes on refusal. Wired into:
- the kanban_complete tool, before the shape check and the parked_by_own_run override;
- `hermes kanban complete` (it calls complete_task without the tool), --force included;
- the dashboard "done" status verb (PATCH and bulk), which is never a worker run.
Left alone: landing handoffs (published_pr), completions with no verdict key, cards naming no core-fork pull.
No override flag: ship refuses these records regardless.

Proof:
- RED on 74b9347149f: 35 of the new tests fail (tool/CLI/dashboard outside approvals complete; helper absent).
- GREEN: tests/tools/test_kanban_review_contract.py 112 passed; 44 kanban complete/review/CLI/dashboard test files,
  970 passed.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, 13): every condition, the check order and each wiring site killed.
- Replay (read-only, default-board replica, completed runs of the last 14 days): 6492 completed runs; 899 are
  verdict-bearing review results on core-pull cards; 894 ran in a dispatched worker run (left alone); 5 were
  recorded outside any worker run (0-second synthesized runs, no claim/spawn event) and would now be refused:
  t_01a1a38501440acb, t_01a1a58d572f7641, t_01a1cce808ae7ea0 (the incident), t_01a1cd4cd17cafcb,
  t_01a1cddfe6588648. All five are review cards.
